## Modifications

The adapted code was substantially rewritten to fit the ServoLoop core
contracts (`servoloop-core::model::Model`, `Message`, `ToolCall`,
`StreamDelta`, `Usage`, `ModelError`):

- No giant static model ID catalog; discovery is fully remote.
- Instance-owned TTL caches keyed by endpoint + account identity (no
  process-global `OnceLock<Mutex<…>>`).
- Secrets are never stored in cache keys or emitted in Debug/log output.
- Models.dev parsing preserves provenance and capability uncertainty
  (unknown capability is never silently upgraded to supported).
- `ProviderSpec` typed protocol/endpoint/env/keyless-policy selection.
- Credential redaction in all error paths.
- reqwest with rustls, no redirects, bounded response/SSE limits.

The extraction renamed the public runtime and provider crates to
`unravel-agent-runtime` and `unravel-agent-providers`. The shared Chat Completions
transport now also supports application-owned headers and raw argument strings,
while canonical model calls retain strict validation. Application branding and
legacy argument repair remain in the consumers.